                <pb facs="0699" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.77/87.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">U. S. S. Petrel</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Puerto Cortés</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Government officer arrived February 6th to seize railroad. I have informed the
                    appointed Government superintendent that I should not permit seizure. Without
                    instructions from Department or Minister, I will enforce this decision. I
                    believe it will not be necessary to use force.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dismukes</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
